### ============================================================
### NoCap Eats — Order Service Manual Tests
### Base: http://localhost:5202  (or via gateway :5000)
### Prerequisite: Identity + Catalog tests done
###   - Customer token
###   - Owner token
###   - A valid restaurantId and menuItemId from Catalog
### ============================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5202

# Paste tokens from Identity tests:
@customerToken = PASTE_CUSTOMER_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
@ownerToken    = PASTE_OWNER_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

# Paste IDs from Catalog tests:
@restaurantId  = PASTE_RESTAURANT_ID_HERE
@menuItemId    = PASTE_MENU_ITEM_ID_HERE

# ── 1. Place orders ───────────────────────────────────────────

### 1a. Place order → 201
# @name placeOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

{
  "restaurantId": "{{restaurantId}}",
  "customerName": "Jane Customer",
  "customerPhone": "+1234567890",
  "deliveryAddress": "789 Customer Lane, London",
  "deliveryNotes": "Please ring the bell",
  "items": [
    {
      "menuItemId": "{{menuItemId}}",
      "name": "Classic Burger Deluxe",
      "quantity": 2,
      "unitPrice": 12.99
    }
  ]
}

### Store order ID from response:
@orderId = PASTE_ORDER_ID_HERE

### 1b. Empty items → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

{
  "restaurantId": "{{restaurantId}}",
  "customerName": "Jane Customer",
  "customerPhone": "+1234567890",
  "deliveryAddress": "789 Customer Lane",
  "deliveryNotes": null,
  "items": []
}

### 1c. No auth → 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "restaurantId": "{{restaurantId}}",
  "customerName": "Jane",
  "customerPhone": "+1234567890",
  "deliveryAddress": "789 Lane",
  "items": [{ "menuItemId": "{{menuItemId}}", "name": "Burger", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 9.99 }]
}

# ── 2. View orders ────────────────────────────────────────────

### 2a. Customer's order history → 200 [1 order]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/my
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 2b. Get specific order → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 2c. Restaurant's incoming orders → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/restaurant-orders/{{restaurantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

# ── 3. Order lifecycle (restaurant drives) ────────────────────

### 3a. Confirm order (Pending → Confirmed) → 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/restaurant-orders/{{orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

{
  "status": 1
}

### 3b. Start preparing (Confirmed → Preparing) → 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/restaurant-orders/{{orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

{
  "status": 2
}

### 3c. Mark ready for pickup (Preparing → ReadyForPickup) → 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/restaurant-orders/{{orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

{
  "status": 3
}

### 3d. Invalid transition (jump from ReadyForPickup → Delivered) → 409 Conflict
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/restaurant-orders/{{orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

{
  "status": 5
}

# ── 4. Cancel order tests ─────────────────────────────────────

### 4a. Place a new order to cancel
# @name cancelableOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

{
  "restaurantId": "{{restaurantId}}",
  "customerName": "Jane Customer",
  "customerPhone": "+1234567890",
  "deliveryAddress": "789 Customer Lane",
  "deliveryNotes": null,
  "items": [
    {
      "menuItemId": "{{menuItemId}}",
      "name": "Classic Burger",
      "quantity": 1,
      "unitPrice": 12.99
    }
  ]
}

@cancelOrderId = PASTE_SECOND_ORDER_ID_HERE

### 4b. Cancel it → 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{cancelOrderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 4c. Cancel again → 409 Conflict (already Cancelled)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{cancelOrderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 4d. Cancel the first order now (in ReadyForPickup) → 409 Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
